    {
      "id": "act.02",
      "criterion": "phrasing",
      "problem": "叫做听力师的听力专家 is circular in Chinese: 听力师 and 听力专家 are effectively the same word, so the gloss that works in English ('a hearing specialist called an audiologist') explains nothing here. The fronted object plus the 由...来设定程序 passive also stretches one idea across a long clause, which a grade 7 reader has to re-read.",
      "suggestion": "就诊时，会由一位听力方面的专业人员（叫做听力师）来给您戴在耳朵外面的言语处理器设定程序。"
    }
  ],
  "verdict": "fail"
